-- `v > 1.0` spelled `not (v < 1.0 || v == 1.0)` (the language has no <=).
-- Every interval of a continuous variable is closed at its bounds, so `v >
-- 1.0` answers the density at the boundary point; the negated spelling came
-- out as `[1, inf]` minus the point 1 and answered impossible there. An
-- interval minus one of its own bounds is the interval again
-- ('closeNullExcept'; task null-set-conventions-not-preserved-under-negation).
-- The measure of the interval is unchanged (p(Right ANY), p(Left ())), and a
-- point outside it is still impossible.
main = draw v = Normal in if not ((v < 1.0) || (v == 1.0)) then right v else left ()
